# EXPERIMENTAL INTEGRITY

Never fabricate, hard-code, or manually manipulate experimental results.

The final 140-question evaluation set must be frozen before final experimentation.

Confidence threshold selection must use separate calibration/development data.

Never tune the final threshold on the final test set.

Save raw results before aggregation.

Experiments must be resumable after interruption.

Never silently overwrite raw experimental results.

Record where applicable:
- dataset/version
- question ID
- architecture
- retrieved evidence
- answer
- verification
- confidence
- threshold
- decision
- model
- model configuration
- temperature
- random seed
- device/GPU
- latency
- run ID

Report non-significant or negative results honestly.

Do not claim that a method improves performance unless the data supports the claim.

Do not change the final sample because the results are unfavorable.